## Targeted Smoke Test

Added:

```text
tests/smokeTestWorkerOperationSerialization.mjs
```

The default mock modes use a temporary runtime fixture and a fake `node-llama-cpp` package so they can run in the sandbox without a real native model.

Optional real-worker modes use the actual local `llama_worker/llama.mjs`, real `node-llama-cpp`, and the local configured model path. They are branch-scoped direct-worker smokes for the serializer boundary, not replacements for full parent lifecycle regression.

Covered mock modes:

```text
mock-reset-session-and-reset-model-ordered
mock-serializer-continues-after-lifecycle-error
mock-shutdown-and-reset-model-ordered
mock-cancel-bypasses-lifecycle-queue
```

Covered optional real-worker modes:

```text
real-direct-reset-session-and-reset-model-ordered
real-direct-shutdown-and-reset-model-ordered
real-orchestrator
```

Key mock coverage:

- `reset_session` and `reset_model` are ordered deterministically.
- The same context is disposed once across serialized `reset_session` / `reset_model` overlap.
- The lifecycle operation chain continues after a lifecycle disposal error.
- `shutdown` and `reset_model` ordering is deterministic when `reset_model` arrives during shutdown disposal.
- `cancel` can still reach an active prompt while lifecycle disposal is running.

The smoke test intentionally keeps prompt execution outside the lifecycle serializer.

Real-worker coverage:

- initializes the actual worker against the local model setup;
- creates a real session through a direct worker prompt;
- posts `reset_session` and `reset_model` back-to-back and verifies `reset_done` precedes `model_reset_done`;
- posts `shutdown` and `reset_model` back-to-back and verifies the expected `reset_model` error is emitted after `shutdown_done`;
- uses direct worker commands to exercise the worker serializer itself rather than only the parent public API, because the parent intentionally prevents some lifecycle overlaps.

